  [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Lint + auto-format
  [38;5;246mESLint plus Prettier, enforced. Stops style debates and catches a class of bugs for near-zero ongoing cost.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Unit tests
  [38;5;246mA runner, a test layout, and one passing fixture. The change-log logic in particular is worth testing — C depends on [39m
  [38;5;246mit being correct.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end tests
  [38;5;246mPlaywright-style browser tests over the real flows. Catches integration breakage; more setup and slower feedback.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] None — keep it bare
  [38;5;246mNo tooling. Fastest to first code, and by far the most expensive to add once there's a codebase to retrofit.[39m
